; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Circle Rosette
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     circle, rotation, rosette, overlapping
; SUMMARY:  Walks circle after circle through the center of the screen, turning between them, to make a rosette.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Every circle starts at the middle of the screen. After each one
;   the turtle turns a little and draws the next. Where the circles
;   cross, petal shapes appear. Three rosettes of different sizes
;   sit inside each other, in different colors.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the numbers in the last three lines, for
;   example  rosette 8 100 [255 0 0]
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a circle drawn by walking: 36 small steps and 10 degree turns
;   * starting every circle from the same point makes them all touch there
;   * overlapping shapes create new shapes (the petals) for free
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Draw 6 circles. Count the petals. Now try 7 and 12.
;   * Use LEFT instead of RIGHT inside CIRCLE. Where do the circles go?
;   * Give every circle its own color with REPCOUNT.
; ============================================================

; A circle that starts and ends where the turtle stands, going
; clockwise. The circle's size depends on the step length:
; 36 steps of :step make a circle about 36 x :step around.
to circle :step
  repeat 36 [forward :step right 10]
end

; Draw :count circles from the middle, turning between them.
to rosette :count :step :color
  setpencolor :color
  repeat :count [
    circle :step
    right 360 / :count
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 245 235]
setpensize 2
rosette 18 23 [40 100 200]
setpensize 3
rosette 12 14 [200 60 120]
rosette 6 7 [240 150 30]
